  "body": "## What and why\n\nAdd the two missing UI regression tests from #3377. The Display-menu test stays unchanged.\n\n- `egui_app::tests::view_names::the_browser_axes_checkbox_leaves_the_ground_grid_visible` opens the Browser View menu and clicks `Show world origin axes`.\n- `egui_app::tests::display_menu::the_viewport_axes_button_leaves_the_ground_grid_visible` clicks the actual viewport navigation button at its live HUD anchor.\n\nEach test starts with axes and Grid on. Each checks that the action hides the axes, leaves Grid on, and keeps the production `ground_grid_lines` result nonempty. No test sets the axes field directly. The tests use the existing shell harness and directory suite. No new test binary or production seam is needed.\n\nThe existing Display-menu test and reverse grid-off/axes-on coverage stay unchanged. The two touched modules contain 11 tests, up from nine. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3377-grid-axes-switch-tests.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\nTested source head: `b0ea9f8bc4e1d02d578cbfefff04c2b3e21be992`.\nBase: upstream `main` at `231b17d8b4ce33d9825b48c69e81952167b74c1c`.\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib leaves_the_ground_grid_visible -- --nocapture`: both new tests pass.\n- Negative control: temporarily restore `!state.show_world_axes || !state.show_grid` in `ground_grid_lines`. Both tests fail at their final grid-output assertion. Restore the production guard. Both tests pass again. The negative control is not in the diff.\n- Display-menu module: eight tests pass. Browser view-switch module: three tests pass.\n- `the_ground_grid_is_a_round_spaced_floor`: passes, including the reverse grid-hidden/axes-visible direction.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 231b17d8b4ce33d9825b48c69e81952167b74c1c`: all 10 selected steps pass on the committed head. UI lib: 1796 passed, eight ignored. The selected integration suites pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passes on the committed head.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --only 'motion light:' --only 'app light:'`: all five test-target steps pass on the committed head. This runs all 11 light twins. The broad all-app `--no-run` preparation step is excluded; each selected target builds normally.\n- `git diff --check`: passes.\n\nLinux checks use a three-job budget. The UI gate reports the software Vulkan adapter, llvmpipe.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nTests and the per-issue decision only. No production behavior, dependency, renderer, geometry, toolpath, post, simulation, collision, or numeric-policy change. No pixel golden changes. No full heavy, release, or example-catalog lane. The standalone app was not launched. No new before/after screenshots are claimed: this test-only change has no visual difference. The harness uses the real controls and production grid generator; it does not prove physical-machine safety.\n\nThe default rustfmt check reports existing formatting differences in these modules. Existing formatting is preserved outside the new tests. No broad formatting rewrite is included.\n\nNo green-CI claim is made. Required rules and actual PR checks are checked separately before handoff. This is an outside-contributor PR for manual maintainer handling, not a counted collaborator review.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3377#issuecomment-7226619228\n\nNo scout was commissioned. Bounded direct searches located the Browser switch, viewport dispatch and HUD anchor, existing Display tests, shell helpers, and ground-grid generator.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3377\n",
